\section{Predictions and future tests}
\label{sec:predictions}

The Echo Equation predicts a coherent, single-frequency residual in late-time growth observables, most visible in redshift-space distortions and galaxy--CMB-lensing cross-correlations. The fundamental scale is
\[
\Delta z \simeq \frac{\pi}{\omega_0}\,,
\]
which is $\approx 0.4$ for the illustrative parameters used here.

Figure~\ref{fig:echo_signature} shows a Phase-20 example included for orientation. A decisive test is a joint fit of RSD and lensing cross-correlations that shares the same echo frequency while allowing independent amplitudes.

